Verse 1:
[F]What heavenly [C]music steals [Dm]o[Gm]ver [C]the [F]sea!
[F]Entrancing the [C]senses like [Dm]sweet [Gm]mel[C7]o[F]dy!
Tis the v[C]oice of the a[F]ngels b[D]orn s[Gm]oft on t[G7]he a[F]ir[C]
[C7]For [F]me they are [C]singing; their [Dm]wel[Gm]come [C7]I[F]hear

Verse 2:
[F]On [C]the banks [Dm]of old [Gm]Jordan, [C]here gazing [F]I stand,
[F]And [C]earnestly [Dm]longing, I [Gm]stretch [C7]forth [F]my hand;
[C]Send [F]a [D]convoy [Gm]of angels, [G7]dear [F]Jesus, [C]I pray!
[C7]Let [F]me [C]join that [Dm]sweet [Gm]music; come, [C7]take [F]me away.

Verse 3:
[F]Though [C]dark are [Dm]the waters [Gm]and [C]rough is [F]the wave,
[F]If [C]Jesus [Dm]permit, the [Gm]wild [C7]surges [F]I'll brave;
[C]For [F]that [D]heavenly [Gm]music [G7]hath [F]ravished [C]me so,
[C7]I [F]must join [C]in [Dm]that chorus! [Gm]I'll [C7]go! let [F]me go!
